    <div class="faq-group" id="pricing">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Pricing and billing</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Is there a design deposit? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. Traditional agencies charge around $3,000 to $5,000 up front, and I charge nothing. Your first $175 payment starts the build, and it's the only fee to begin.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What does $175 a month cover? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">It covers custom design, a custom-coded build of up to 10 pages, hosting, the security certificate (SSL), unlimited content updates, and direct support from me. It also covers a phone-first design, the groundwork for local search (on-page and local SEO), and ongoing security monitoring.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why is there a 12-month minimum? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I do the full custom build with nothing down, and the 12-month minimum is how the numbers work out on my side. After the first year, the plan goes month to month, and you can cancel with 30 days' written notice.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I need to cancel early? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The remaining monthly payments are due under the service agreement. I usually find a fair way to work it out, but the written agreement governs.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I buy out the plan to own the code? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. On the monthly plan, I own the code, and there's no code buyout. Your domain stays in your name, and you control it.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What gets billed at $100 an hour? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Work outside the plan costs $100 an hour, and I send you a written estimate first. Examples include a custom calculator, a booking system from another company, and an email-marketing template. Moving content from your old site is part of the build. An extra page beyond the 10 included costs $100 per page.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I miss a monthly payment? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Cards fail sometimes. I email you, and you have 15 days to update the card or pay another way, with your site online the whole time. After that, I check in personally before doing anything more, so a stuck payment never turns into a stuck website.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Are the monthly payments a business tax deduction? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">For almost every U.S. and Canadian small business, web hosting and design fees are an ordinary business expense, fully deductible in the year you pay them. I'm not a tax professional, so check with your accountant. On request, I send an itemized year-end receipt your bookkeeper will recognize.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group" id="website">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">The website</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How long does it take to build my site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Most sites are designed, built, and launched in two to three weeks. Work begins when your first payment clears, and the timing depends mostly on how soon you send your logo, photos, and service details.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How many pages do I get? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The plan includes up to 10 pages, and each extra page, for another service, another location, or new content, costs $100 per page. Most service businesses need six to eight: home, about, services, service area, FAQ, and contact.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I own my website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You own your domain: it's registered in your name, and you control it. On the monthly plan, I own the code and host it for you, which is how I can build the site with nothing down. If you cancel, the site goes offline at the end of your term. There's no export of the site and no code buyout.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I update the site myself? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You don't need to, because unlimited updates are part of the plan: email or text me what you want changed, and I make the change. If you'd like a simple editor for writing blog posts yourself (a CMS), I can add one.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What about my existing site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I time the launch so there's no downtime between the old site and the new one. Once the new site is live, you can take the old one offline or archive it privately, whichever you prefer.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I have a blog? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, and it's part of the standard plan. It comes with a blog index, a post template, a table of contents that stays on screen, a reading-progress bar, share buttons, and an RSS feed. New posts count as content updates.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group" id="process">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Process and support</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What's the discovery call like? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">It's free and takes 20 to 30 minutes on Google Meet, or by phone if you prefer. I learn about your business and goals and answer your questions. If I'm the right fit, I send a plain-English service agreement and we get started. The call is optional, and you can sign up without one.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Who will I be working with? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Me, Jon Ajinga, the founder, in Colorado Springs. I write your code and answer your emails myself, with no account managers, offshore developers, or handoffs in between. The <a href="/about/" class="inline-link">about page</a> covers the rest.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I don't have a logo or photos? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I don't design logos, so a logo needs to come from you or a designer you hire. For photos, I can help you find a local photographer, or work with the photos you have and fill gaps with carefully chosen stock images.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How fast is support? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I make routine content updates quickly on most business days. Emergencies, such as the site being down, wrong information being live, or an urgent correction, jump the queue and get handled fast. Email, phone, and text all reach me directly.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you work with businesses outside Colorado? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. I work with small businesses across the U.S. and Canada, fully remotely, with the same quality, schedule, and price wherever you are.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group" id="seo">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Search and speed</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you guarantee Google rankings? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Nobody can guarantee specific rankings, so be skeptical of anyone who promises them. I guarantee the foundation: a fast, accessible, well-built site with clean on-page SEO, your business details marked up for Google (local-business schema), proper sitemaps, and strong Core Web Vitals (Google's page-experience scores). Rankings grow from it with time, content, and reviews.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What speed score should I expect? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Every site I build scores 95 to 100 on Google's speed test (PageSpeed Insights), on both mobile and desktop, with every Core Web Vital in the green.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will my site be accessible? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. I build every site to meet WCAG 2.2 AA, the common accessibility standard, with strong contrast, visible focus outlines, and full keyboard navigation. It's written into the code from the start instead of added with a plug-in.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will I get Google Analytics? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">By default, I set up two privacy-friendly ways to count visitors: <span class="term" data-term="Counts visits and popular pages without cookies or personal tracking, so your site needs no cookie banner.">a visitor counter</span> and <span class="term" data-term="Free visitor statistics from the hosting network, collected without cookies.">the hosting network's own statistics</span>. Both are fast and need no cookie banner. I can add Google Analytics 4 alongside them or instead, at no extra cost.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you set up my Google Business Profile? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, setting it up or reviewing it is part of every launch. I match your name, address, and phone number to the site, choose the right categories, list your service areas, and get the business verified. After launch, I revisit it every quarter to keep hours, photos, and posts fresh.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Will you write blog posts for me, or do I? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The blog is yours to write by default, since you know your trade best. If you'd rather not write, I offer ghostwritten posts at $100 an hour, and an average 1,200-word post takes two to three hours. Most owners choose a mix: they outline, I draft, and they edit.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group" id="forms">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Forms and operational pages</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What forms does my site come with? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Every site comes with a contact form, sent through <span class="term" data-term="An outside service that delivers form messages straight to your email, with no server to maintain and no cookies.">a spam-resistant form service</span>, and a matching thank-you page. I can also add forms for your trade, such as emergency requests for HVAC and plumbing, free-inspection requests for roofing, bid forms for contractors, and booking forms for home inspectors. The <a href="/sample-forms/" class="inline-link">sample forms gallery</a> shows eight industry examples.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What are operational pages, and do they count against my page limit? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">They're the standard pages every professional site needs: the Privacy Policy, Accessibility Statement, Terms of Use, Contact, Thank-You, Style Guide, and Sitemap. Every build includes all of them, and none count against your 10 pages, so you're covered legally, ethically, and technically from launch day.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What technical files come with the site? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You won't see them day to day, but they do useful work: <code>robots.txt</code> guides search engines, <code>humans.txt</code> credits who built the site, <code>sitemap.xml</code> goes to Google for you, and <code>security.txt</code> tells researchers how to report a problem. You also get a branded <code>404</code> page, favicons for every device, and preview images for shared links (Open Graph and Twitter cards). It's all set up during the build and needs no upkeep from you.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How do I request a content change once the site is live? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The fastest way is the <a href="/content-update/" class="inline-link">content update form</a> in your client portal, because your request arrives organized and ready to act on. You can also email me at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.email }}</a> or call or text <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if the site is down and I need help right now? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Call or text me first at <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>. Then, if you can, fill out the <a href="/emergency/" class="inline-link">emergency support form</a> with what's happening, when it started, and any error messages on screen. Emergencies skip the queue.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I give feedback on the design while you're building? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Please do. That's what the preview link is for, and the <a href="/design-feedback/" class="inline-link">design feedback form</a> keeps every note in one place. You can have as many rounds as you need, with no charge per change, because I'd rather get the site right than get it fast.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do you pay referral fees? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, in account credit rather than cash. If you refer a business and they become a client, I credit one month of hosting to your account, and if you're not a client yet, I hold the credit until you sign on. The <a href="/refer/" class="inline-link">referral form</a> takes about a minute.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-group" id="demos">
      <h2 class="faq-group-title">Demos and samples</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
